# Forest Scatter Benchmark — Valtellina (Terrain3D)

Runtime, not editor. Scene `scenes/real_terrain_valtellina_forest_test.tscn`.
Renderer: Forward+ (Vulkan 1.4.335), GPU AMD Radeon RX 9070 XT (RADV GFX1201).
Requested window 1400x1000. Project uses `window/stretch/mode="canvas_items"` +
`aspect="expand"`, so measured logical viewport = (1152, 822), physical = (1400, 1000).
All runs below use `--no-vsync` (DisplayServer.VSYNC_DISABLED) at a fixed camera
(medium oblique over the forest). Frame time is the real uncapped headroom; the
old vsync-capped ~94 FPS figure was display-refresh-limited, not GPU-limited.

## Progressive counts (default bounded bake `trees.bin`, 2000 m area)

`--limit=N` limits resident instances. `visible` = instances in cell batches whose
AABB centre is inside the camera frustum (submitted/visible estimate).

| resident | visible | FPS | avg ms | median ms | p95 ms | draw_calls | objects | primitives |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0    | 0    | 595.7 | 1.68 | 1.03 | 1.35 | 103 | 245 | 744,784 |
| 1000 | 999  | 590.0 | 1.69 | 1.05 | 1.27 | 139 | 281 | 754,554 |
| 3000 | 2999 | 585.5 | 1.71 | 1.06 | 1.27 | 209 | 351 | 773,957 |
| 5903 | 5533 | 581.6 | 1.72 | 1.06 | 1.32 | 251 | 393 | 801,675 |

Frame time is essentially flat (~1.7 ms) from 0 → 5903 instances. The scene is
dominated by terrain/base overhead; the instanced forest is GPU-light. Draw calls
scale 103 → 251 as batches are added, but the cost is tiny (uncapped ~580–596 FPS).

## Stress profile (separate area, same configs)

`--bake=res://assets/forest_test/trees_stress.bin`. Baked with `--size=4000`
(4000 m area) at the same `minimum_spacing=15`, `density=1.0`, seed 1337, height
20–30 m. This is a separate stress profile/area, NOT the default world population.

| resident | visible | FPS | avg ms | median ms | p95 ms | draw_calls | objects | primitives |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 15068 | 7980 | 564.9 | 1.77 | 1.11 | 1.45 | 459 | 601 | 847,471 |

At 15068 instances the scene still runs uncapped at ~565 FPS (1.77 ms), draw calls
459. GPU is not the bottleneck. Culling is active: 7980/15068 resident instances are
in the frustum at this camera (the rest are culled by the tight per-cell AABBs).

## Notes

- `visible` is an estimate from `Camera3D.is_position_in_frustum()` on each cell
  batch AABB centre; the exact renderer-culled count is not exposed by Godot.
- All measurements are runtime with vsync disabled. Do not overclaim from the
  earlier vsync-capped ~94 FPS reading; the uncapped values above are the real
  headroom.
- Stress results are distinct from the default bounded test. The default
  `trees.bin` remains the bounded 2000 m / 5903-tree bake.
